  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening CSOs as inclusive actors of good governance and development in Sierra Leone</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The action fully contributes to the global objective of this call to `strengthen local CSOs&#xbf; engagement as actors of good governance and development in Sierra Leone&#xbf;, specifically in relation to youth, women, vulnerable and marginalised people (lot 1). The action builds on the lead MAPCO and co-applicants MUWODA and APT&#xbf;s experience of highly collaborative and impactful EU actions strengthening local CSOs under the CSO-LA programme in Kenema (45 CSOs 2018-21) and Pujehun (19 CBOs 2019-22). Combining the experience of MAPCO and MUWODA, a women-led organisation, this action builds on the gains made in the districts and chiefdoms, targeting primarily new CSOs (representing women, youth and PWD) in chiefdoms previously worked in; improving the capacity of CSOs to sustain themselves, engage with and make demands of local customary and state authorities, and ensure equal representation of women, youth and PWD. With a specific objective of `Strengthened CSOs&#xbf; engagement as inclusive actors of good governance and development in Pujehun and Kenema Districts, with improved capacity to work collectively as a coordinated civil society network and to sustainably meet and represent the needs of marginalised groups&#xbf;, the action is closely aligned to SO3 of this call: Strengthened capacity of local CSOs to engage in gender equality, youth inclusion and strengthened capacity of local women&#xbf;s and youth partner CSOs. It also contributes to building the capacity of local CSOs to promote an enabling environment at local levels (SO2) through which influence can be achieved.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
